#   lsd (database rebuild): registers 6 extension points, 191 apps, ONE app extension, no framework extension at all.
# The 6 points are the .appexpt files of /System/Library/ExtensionKit/ExtensionPoints. The other 138 extension points of
# iOS 16.7 (com.apple.posterkit.provider, com.apple.widgetkit-extension, share/keyboard/intents/notification/...) are defined
# only in /System/Library/xpc/extensions.plist. ExtensionFoundation (-[EXExtensionPointEnumerator initWithSDKDictionary:urls:
# config:]) reads that file with +[NSDictionary _EX_dictionaryWithSignedURL:error:] when the feature flag
# ExtensionKit/enforce_xpc_cache_code_signing is on (it is, in /System/Library/FeatureFlags/Domain/ExtensionKit.plist) and the
# process holds com.apple.private.amfi.can-check-trust-cache (lsd and installd do): detached signature + the IOKit service
# 'AppleMobileFileIntegrity' selector 6 'is this cdhash in the trust cache'. The port kernel has no such service and no trust
# cache (bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c), so the file is rejected, LaunchServices never learns the extension points, and
# InstalledContentLibrary drops every app extension whose point is unknown (129 in /Applications + the framework ones, among
